<!-- Aura-SOC - rule 100945 (level 12). Domain: suricata,ids,
     Naming convention and load-order trap: see rules/README.md -->
<group name="suricata,ids,">

  <!-- TLS handshake towards anonymous serverless hosting: modern C2 fronting.

       The native rule 86604 decodes `event_type: tls` at level 0, so the SNI
       never reaches an alert. That is the right default - logging every TLS
       handshake of the estate would drown the SIEM - but it makes one specific
       case invisible, and it is the case that matters.

       Cloudflare Workers, Cloudflare Tunnel quick tunnels, ngrok and their
       equivalents give an attacker a free, throwaway, TLS-terminated endpoint on
       a reputable IP range. Blocking by IP is useless (172.64.0.0/13 is shared
       with half the web) and reputation feeds rate the domain as clean. The SNI
       is the only discriminator available on the wire.

       No legitimate server-to-server traffic in this estate calls a *.workers.dev
       or a *.trycloudflare.com. A developer testing their own Worker from a
       workstation is the expected false positive - hence the exclusion below,
       to be filled per deployment rather than left open.

       Found in production 2026-08-11: /tmp/.cache-update.py on debian (LAB500)
       beaconing to cipherfall-c2.<compte>.workers.dev every 2-3 seconds. The
       firewall saw nothing (LAB500 pass rule was not logged), the DNS pipeline
       was empty, and the case had already been opened on host telemetry alone -
       the network side of the same incident was completely dark.

       Level 12: one handshake is enough to open a case. -->

  <rule id="100945" level="12">
    <if_sid>86604</if_sid>
    <field name="tls.sni" type="pcre2">\.(?:workers\.dev|trycloudflare\.com|ngrok\.io|ngrok-free\.app|loca\.lt|serveo\.net|telebit\.io|pagekite\.me)$</field>
    <description>C2 over anonymous serverless hosting: TLS to $(tls.sni) from $(src_ip) ($(in_iface))</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1071.001</id>
      <id>T1090.004</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>command_and_control,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
